      {
        "kind": "grantFact",
        "person": "holmes",
        "fact": "holmes_heath_road_dust"
      },
      {
        "kind": "grantFact",
        "person": "holmes",
        "fact": "holmes_victualler_deduction"
      },
      {
        "kind": "grantFact",
        "person": "holmes",
        "fact": "holmes_observation_vs_inference"
      },
      {
        "kind": "playBeat",
        "beats": [
          "Holmes read the street aloud for me: the licensed victualler by the pillar box had kept his daughter out an hour past the time her mother allowed; the man under the lamp had walked in from Hampstead that morning to save the fare.",
          "When I said he could not know the man had walked, he raised the opera glass once more, then set it down on the mantel: the man's boots were white to the ankle with the pale dust of the Heath road. \"That is a fact. That he walked is an inference. You will note the difference, Watson, because nobody else in London does.\""
        ]
      }
    ],
    "once": true
  },
