      {
        "kind": "grantFact",
        "person": "holmes",
        "fact": "holmes_monograph"
      },
      {
        "kind": "setDisposition",
        "person": "holmes",
        "disposition": "warm"
      },
      {
        "kind": "playBeat",
        "beats": [
          "I called it a parlour trick any man might do who had nothing better to do with his evening, and Holmes turned from the window with the look of a man offered a diversion.",
          "\"Any man. Very well: a wager. Read me two people in that street. Read both correctly and I shall not touch the violin before midnight; fail, and you shall read my monograph upon the ashes of the various tobaccos, all hundred and forty varieties, plates included.\"",
          "\"The old fellow on the kerb by the cab rank. And the clergyman outside the chemist's. When you have your man, give me your reading, and I shall hold you to it.\""
        ]
      }
    ],
    "once": true
  },
  {
    "id": "reading_as_deduction",
    "trigger": {
      "kind": "action",
