  {
    "id": "soldier_reading",
    "trigger": {
      "kind": "disclosed",
      "fact": "holmes_soldier_grandchild",
      "from": "holmes",
      "to": "player"
    },
    "when": {
      "flagsNone": [
        "verdict_given"
      ]
    },
    "effects": [
      {
        "kind": "setFlag",
        "flag": "soldier_read"
      },
      {
        "kind": "grantFact",
        "person": "holmes",
        "fact": "holmes_watsons_service"
      },
      {
        "kind": "playBeat",
        "beats": [
          "I gave him my reading of the old man: an infantryman by the way he stood, for cavalrymen stand otherwise; Indian service, and not lately, for the colour had gone into the skin; an old fracture of the left thigh, set in a hurry by a regimental surgeon and healed short, a walk I had watched men learn at the base hospital at Peshawar; and probably a sergeant. Holmes heard me out, and then conceded it."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "once": true
  },
  {
    "id": "clergyman_reading_right",
    "trigger": {
      "kind": "disclosed",
      "fact": "holmes_actor_reading",
      "from": "holmes",
      "to": "player"
    },
    "when": {
      "flagsAll": [
        "greasepaint_seen"
      ]
    },
    "effects": [
      {
        "kind": "setFlag",
        "flag": "clergyman_read"
      },
      {
        "kind": "setFlag",
        "flag": "clergyman_read_right"
      },
      {
        "kind": "playBeat",
        "beats": [
          "I gave him my reading of the clergyman: no curate at all, but a man who would like to be thought one. That was greasepaint at his hairline, and he was learning a part, not a lesson: an actor between performances who had not changed out of his costume.",
          "Holmes looked at me for so long that I began to fear some fresh error, and then said I had it exactly: a West End house, a melodrama with a clergyman in it, and he was not wanted until the second act."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "once": true
  },
  {
    "id": "clergyman_reading_wrong",
    "trigger": {
      "kind": "disclosed",
      "fact": "holmes_actor_reading",
      "from": "holmes",
      "to": "player"
    },
    "when": {
      "flagsNone": [
        "greasepaint_seen"
      ]
    },
    "effects": [
      {
        "kind": "setFlag",
        "flag": "clergyman_read"
      },
      {
        "kind": "playBeat",
        "beats": [
          "I gave him my reading of the clergyman: a curate from a poor country parish, by his coat, up for the holiday and getting tomorrow's lesson by heart.",
          "\"Ah,\" said Holmes, very gently, and bade me look again, through the glass: a brownish line of greasepaint at the hairline, too even to be dirt, and a thin paper script in a coloured wrapper. I felt foolish.",
          "\"You saw a black coat and a white tie, and stopped looking, because you had your answer. It is the commonest error in the world, and the most expensive.\""
        ]
      }
    ],
    "once": true
  },
